commit 283e48d71dd0a4dd4102b755aaac3e6996f4520e
Author: zurich-maps-2 <zurich-maps-2@swarm.local>
Date:   Sun Oct 18 22:12:42 2026 +0000

    maps-2: unflake the IIIF viewer checks in the browser harness

    The three viewer checks read `img.src` after fixed sleeps (1800-2500 ms).
    The region request is debounced and `img.src` only changes once the new
    bitmap decodes, so e-rara latency above the sleep made 'viewer pans with the
    arrow keys' fail intermittently (reproduced with a CDP probe: the pan request
    settled after ~0.9 s in one run, later than 1.8 s in the failing run).
    Replaced the sleeps with a waitForViewer() poll on the real state (decoded +
    src predicate); it also reports the last snapshot when a check fails.

    Verified: node scripts/browser-check.mjs -> 34/34 checks.

